                    description: "Mr. Sumit Sapru is the CEO of Shapoorji Pallonji Real Estate (SPRE).<br/><br/> He has been leading business operations and implementing business strategies that drive growth and profitability for SPRE with P&L responsibility.<br/><br/> Sumit has over two decades of multi-faceted experience in conceptualization, analysing, and execution of turnkey projects and assignments involving business analytics and profits.<br/><br/> Sumit joined SPRE in 2017 and, since then, has been instrumental in strategy development, fundraising, investor management, and techno-commercial discussions, besides running business operations for the company’s projects.<br/><br/> Before SPRE, Sumit was Head of the New Business Group at Tata Housing. He was responsible for setting up new business lines for Tata Housing, like senior living, affordable housing JVs with IFC and CDC, real estate expansion across Africa, PPP projects, and a real estate service company.<br/><br/> Sumit started his corporate career at Wockhardt as Manager of Business Development, responsible for the SEZ acquisition of the group, and subsequently operated a private equity-funded media startup.<br/><br/> Before his corporate career, Sumit served the Indian Army as part of the Special Forces and was awarded the Chief of Army Staff Commendation Medal twice.<br/><br/> In terms of education, Sumit graduated from the National Defence Academy (Jawaharlal Nehru University (JNU) and is a post-graduate in International Business from the Indian Institute of Foreign Trade (IIFT, New Delhi) and an alumnus of IIM Calcutta.",
                },
                // "sunita-khanna": {
